WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
[Instrumental music: Night Owl by Broke For Free]
Photos. Vectors. Possibility. A native creative studio for Linux.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Find the light. Editable exposure and colour balance.
Original and Omuse 0.7.0 photo exports are compared.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Shape the contrast. Channel mixing and curves
turn the flower into warm monochrome.

4
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Choose the focus. Gaussian blur through a retained layer mask
softens the scene around the subject.

5
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Change the feeling. A gradient map remaps the palette
while keeping the flower’s natural detail.

6
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Shape every idea. Pen, Nodes and Move share the canvas.
Edit curves, anchors and multiple styled objects.

7
00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Pixels to possibilities. Trace locally and refine editable curves.
Detail controls create solid-colour approximations.

8
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Make colour deliberate. Target Colour Uniformity,
visible colour swatches and Camera Raw controls.

9
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:18.000
One idea. A whole collection. Editable pages and a shared brand.
Keep the editable .omuse project.

10
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Your brief. Your choice. Choose a connection and review what you keep.
Offline interface demo; no new AI request.

11
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Give it motion. An actual Omuse page animation,
followed by the Motion workspace. Export MP4 or GIF.

12
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Ready to share. Export the content set
and keep the editable project.

13
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Stay in flow. Ctrl+K searches tools, commands and shortcuts.
Make shortcuts your own.

14
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Make the next thing. github.com/Sugata-Software/Omuse
Music: Night Owl by Broke For Free, edited under CC BY 3.0.
